+/**
+ * @file
+ * The console's hardware video decoder: H.264 on the console's own video chip.
+ *
+ * The chip is reached through a system module the application loads at
+ * startup. It wants its access units in the graphics memory, its memory
+ * mapped in a particular way, and it aborts the process when it refuses
+ * work.
+ *
+ * The pictures come out as NV12 (or P010 for ten bit), which the caller
+ * hands on like any other frame.
+ *
+ * The layout of the chip's structures and the way it wants its memory come
+ * from the VLC for PS5 port (ZiZc3/VLC, GPL-2.0-or-later).
+ */
